docs/architecture/core-types.md:41:`CodeBlock.signature_span` is the byte range of the declaration's head, of which `symbol_signature` is the one-line form: it starts at the first byte after any decorators, attributes and doc comments (so `export` and `pub` are inside it) and ends after the `{` that opens a block body, after the `}` of a body with nothing in it, at the start of an expression body or an initializer, or at the end of a declaration with no body. It is `Some` exactly when `symbol_signature` is and lies inside `span`. The snippet leaves out a matched line whose text lies inside it.
